<title>EGYPT: Egypt pound interbank market quiet and liquid.</title>
<headline>Egypt pound interbank market quiet and liquid.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overnight interbank rates on the Egyptian pound were unchanged on Thursday at 9-7/8 percent in a very liquid private-sector market, but most bankers said they did not carry out any deals.</p>
<p>One banker said he heard rates of 10-1/4 percent. One-week rates were quoted at 9-3/4 to 10-1/8 percent, easing from 9-7/8 percent on Wednesday, bankers said.</p>
<p>Public sector banks maintained their minimum overnight lending rates at 10-1/2 percent.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
